# The cube from offer to drop, a whole match won, the Crawford game, and
# a match that survives a relaunch at each stage. Two players pass the
# reader, because only a person can drop a double; the computer always
# takes. The sweep pins the dice to seed 7, and a relaunch starts the
# seeded dice over, so the rolls below follow from these exact steps.
wait-for Backgammon
tap-id game-more
tap Match settings
expect Fixture dice, seed 7.
expect Against the computer
tap Two players
tap-id length-3
expect White 0 · Black 0
clean
shot match-settings-two-players
tap Play
expect This match now plays to 3 points. Tap Roll to begin.
tap Roll
expect Black opened with 4 and 6.
expect Black to play
# The board turns to Black; Black's 13 is White's 12th point.
tap-id point-11
tap-id point-17
tap-id point-11
tap-id point-15
expect Pass the reader to White.
expect 1 · either side may double
clean
shot pass-to-white
tap Double
expect Offer the cube at 2?
tap Offer double
expect White offers the cube at 2
expect Black may take and play on for 2 points
clean
shot cube-offered
# A pending offer is saved, so a relaunch puts the question back.
restart
wait-for White offers the cube at 2
tap Drop
expect Drop White's double?
expect This ends the game and cannot be undone.
clean
shot drop-confirm
tap Cancel
expect White offers the cube at 2
tap Take
expect Black takes. White to roll.
expect 2 · Black owns it
tap Double
expect Only the cube owner may double.
tap Roll
expect White rolled 4 and 6.
tap Roll
expect The dice are already rolled. 4 and 6 left to play.
# Dice in play survive a relaunch too.
restart
wait-for Resumed saved game. 4 and 6 left to play.
tap-id point-12
tap-id point-6
tap-id point-12
tap-id point-8
expect Pass the reader to Black.
# Black owns the cube, redoubles to 4, and White drops: 2 points to Black.
tap Double
tap Offer double
expect Black offers the cube at 4
tap Drop
tap Drop cube
expect Black won this game.
expect White 0 · Black 2 · first to 3
expect White dropped the cube. The game was worth 2 points.
expect Next game
# A finished game has nothing to take back.
expect-missing Undo
clean
shot game-won
restart
wait-for Black won the saved game.
expect Next game
tap-id game-more
tap Turn history
expect Black won a game worth 2 points on a drop.
expect White 13/7 13/9
expect Black 13/7 13/9
clean
shot history-after-drop
tap-id 4294967295
# Black is a point from the match, so the next game is the Crawford game.
tap Next game
expect Crawford game: nobody may double. Tap Roll to begin.
tap Double
expect Nobody can double before the opening roll.
tap Roll
expect Black opened with 4 and 6.
tap-id point-11
tap-id point-17
tap-id point-11
tap-id point-15
tap Double
expect Nobody may double in the Crawford game.
expect no doubling this game
clean
shot crawford
# Starting again mid-match asks first; the length can change only then.
tap-id game-more
tap New game
expect Start a new game?
tap Start new game
expect White 0 · Black 0
tap-id game-more
tap Match settings
tap-id length-1
tap Play
expect This match now plays to 1 point. Tap Roll to begin.
tap Roll
expect White opened with 3 and 2.
tap-id point-12
tap-id point-9
tap-id point-12
tap-id point-10
tap Double
tap Offer double
tap Drop
tap Drop cube
expect Black won the match 1–0.
expect White 0 · Black 1 · first to 1
expect New game
clean
shot match-won
restart
wait-for Black won the saved match.
tap New game
expect Tap Roll. The higher die moves first.
expect-missing Start a new game?
# Back against the computer, which takes every double it is offered.
tap-id game-more
tap Match settings
tap Against the computer
tap Play
tap Roll
expect Computer opened with
tap Double
tap Offer double
expect Computer takes. Your roll.
restart
wait-for Resumed saved game. Your roll.
clean
shot solo-cube-taken
# The cube line names the sides the way the score does.
expect 2 · Computer owns it
